<title>SPAIN: Spain's Baron de Ley starts trade at 2,800 pta.</title>
<headline>Spain's Baron de Ley starts trade at 2,800 pta.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Spanish winery Baron de Ley  started trade for the first time on Wednesday at 2,800 pesetas, versus a public offering price of 2,350 pesetas, dealers said.</p>
<p>At 0840 GMT shares were at 2,870 pesetas.</p>
<p>The public offering price was 100 pesetas above the non-mandatory maximum price initially set by the sale managers.</p>
<p>Spanish bourse regulations set a maximum share rise of 15 percent from the opening price in one day.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 8340</p>
